course: dictionary
lesson: 15120
title: Sami: a people, a language, a name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «The Sami people have lived in the far north of Norway for a very long time.» Here Sami is a people, because the words people, Norway and the far north tell you where they live.
explain: «Many Sami families herd reindeer across the snowy hills.» Herding reindeer is something the Sami people do, so this sentence is about a group of people and their way of life.
explain: «Some Sami speak Sami languages at home.» The word languages is a clue. Sami languages are the languages spoken by the Sami people. Now look at «Sami kicked the ball to his friend.» Nobody kicks a people or a language. Sami is a person's first name here, and the capital letter tells you it is a name.
fact: The Sami are an Indigenous people, which means they have lived in their land for a very long time, before many others arrived.
fact: The Sami live in the far north of Norway, Sweden, Finland and Russia. Their area is called Sápmi.
fact: Many Sami people have herded reindeer, and some still do today.
fact: Sami is also a first name for a person, used in Finland and in Arabic-speaking countries.
fact: Say Sami, not the old word Lapp, because many people find Lapp rude.
exercise: «The Sami people live in the far north of Norway and Sweden.» Where do the Sami live? | In the middle of a desert | Only in one big city | Far south of Spain | *The far north of Norway and Sweden
exercise: «Sami kicked the ball to his friend.» What is Sami in this sentence? | *A person's first name | A language | A kind of reindeer | A cold northern place
exercise: «Many Sami families herd reindeer across the snowy hills.» What do many Sami families do? | Sell ice cream on the beach | *Herd reindeer | Grow bananas in greenhouses | Fly planes over the sea
test: What is Sápmi? | A river in Spain | A type of Sami song | *The area of the far north where the Sami live | A shop that sells reindeer
test: In our world cultures lesson we learned about Sami culture. Which of these is part of Sami culture? | Penguins on the ice | A camel race in the desert | Sandcastles on a beach | *Colourful gákti clothes and joik songs
exam: In «Ella's friend Sami is from Finland», what does Sami mean? | *A first name for a person | A language | A reindeer | The far north of Norway
